#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent to a Trajectory Given an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8928a0bf-8c54-5640-86e0-040f5be3c760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}19 \\\\ \\frac{37}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164150} {:answer/id #uuid "bf88ff78-0f7d-5f01-aa97-89b7d88561c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164151} {:answer/id #uuid "daf0c5ca-090e-5f08-8c33-bc81df2efa95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{29}{2} \\\\ \\frac{11}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164152} {:answer/id #uuid "12df3afc-4f13-5cbf-8d2e-5c282647ae34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{59}{4} \\\\ \\frac{11}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164153} {:answer/id #uuid "3870f3a8-b890-53a7-9599-dfd15a233842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{37}{2} \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3870f3a8-b890-53a7-9599-dfd15a233842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{37}{2} \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164154} :answer-field/id #uuid "8428bd41-76ca-5b45-a369-cccb3b8fa584" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "923e8ea5-006a-5c4e-a94f-6a9b7c029dba" :question/math-academy-id "q-331276" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{59}{4} \\\\ \\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{59}{4} \\\\ \\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2(\\frac{59}{4})-2(\\frac{11}{2}) \\\\ 2(\\frac{59}{4})-3(\\frac{11}{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{2} \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Nullclines of a System of Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d3d593-5d00-5de8-bf14-024bdae09a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164156} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ea43de-b2d5-53bd-a777-23c39d5e8510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164157} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1bcf3d-c60e-552d-b102-1bedd29809f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164158} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb66478-cb47-5059-9571-3f19991ac349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb66478-cb47-5059-9571-3f19991ac349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164159} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f2747ca-0cbc-5816-ba92-1c8296bc5a91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493bbf94-36f1-59ba-b77d-add5e858e08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− (1)/(2)x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164161} {:answer/id #uuid "62a2b78b-594e-5182-8476-e2a000029918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/(2)x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164162} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4a6a5e-2249-500a-93b8-7970247e5c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− (2)/(3)x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164163} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0d19a7-df29-57eb-b964-9b173d76e8f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/(2)x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d4a6a5e-2249-500a-93b8-7970247e5c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− (2)/(3)x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164163} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a34920e-5fac-5eb9-be07-5761d3174a5b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c96b74a-d34e-5ce3-b63d-86dac5a4ffc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-331282" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x-2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x+3y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{2}{3}x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/6ba5066fd4ddc43491c3d007355e0b64c84d449d6462812aa4c8ca0450887a8b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent to a Trajectory Given an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f8be66a-630c-5c07-b669-698561814a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379799} {:answer/id #uuid "6958974a-cb9b-5415-81c1-e753d1d2c88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379800} {:answer/id #uuid "f09121ea-3b99-556c-917c-3479af3d2ed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379801} {:answer/id #uuid "0d218137-14ef-59f8-ac5d-cf6181c3ea36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379802} {:answer/id #uuid "810b9991-6bbc-578d-a5a2-932f87988609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "810b9991-6bbc-578d-a5a2-932f87988609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379803} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ba321af-28d5-5d6d-a0f1-8e3ed39a4281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "556ea4da-7963-5f2a-ac1a-0192abc563d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-332627" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =9[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1(10)+1(8) \\\\ 1(10)+1(8)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Trajectory Given a Starting Point and the Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a858cd-ae80-5d80-bf6d-237251530561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/d49ef93ba4beb20d33346f90cab0d2b0c6cd2833b10a3390facfdf2d070e0c18.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379806} {:answer/id #uuid "1ecd0a32-87c3-5cbc-8e28-986f294bd0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/0c3abb4df91d6f9c3da4eb5394eea9a73df8eed6a782ed0eccede9e946e5836e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379807} {:answer/id #uuid "397b6364-a4a8-5fe9-891d-1bf703726789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/fa6cf07dc92efbd6eca770d4c9af2aa3eaa312d585e2a44169967e346a236198.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379808} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec2d49d-7b85-5f91-966a-fc566b801436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/41a653adc61eec8ab01704b2171e14c8dd0454880db7c643929142f7544a23c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379809} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7597d8-2ddf-594c-b52c-d8e3874e8d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/813739fde6ecbd8b97d37cd500f104fbd0aafd6c3247e38569ed1b2e16d7d351.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ecd0a32-87c3-5cbc-8e28-986f294bd0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/0c3abb4df91d6f9c3da4eb5394eea9a73df8eed6a782ed0eccede9e946e5836e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379807} :answer-field/id #uuid "771b1121-3d1a-512a-b1ce-5bac27ed58a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8ff40f4-1d1b-5478-9383-2934565c286e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332873" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/d9103a8e40d3040b711d0bcfc8cf759d6515ba7d0ae060239d203940e4b09daf.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point and go along with the flow (slightly downward and to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $y$-nullcline, where the tangents are horizontal.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/146fd1dd846803a8ee5684756a1ddf92b4236b49ad3082bd2397b07eb30671aa.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues to the right and gradually turns upward.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/cf3b24d0c6249d7b60803ea62a06c160b987b2892d4e56f91f0001d276ec4838.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory keeps going to the right and slightly upward to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/58cefcb6d77335a6dd54aba7bdffdb19024fd8c6aab0659389097ba1ced6d6a0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Trajectory Given a Starting Point and the Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8a4f8b2-3825-5b5a-b35f-0302db04c054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/b3f8771ae6044e667c42c48f92800117ff55e494c6e2521bca5071f206e234ef.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379813} {:answer/id #uuid "00717900-8531-5b0a-ae37-ccf392faada5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/4c4388dd27a0306f274674c2fa41b042bbe03a43dec59e7f93d02d0cab35ebb2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379814} {:answer/id #uuid "564cb34b-ce5f-5da5-942c-862cb3de4ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/d0601c8b18b3a3b0b8c9388818b750c3d4cd36c89c1d4b854fc145a437d34ae0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379815} {:answer/id #uuid "2442b6d9-06cb-5e4a-9536-6fff9833d38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/fe487e378dd633f91ee7cf1243312631695a5c750f8c0a0c888c9f2c86268ed3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379816} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc2c5bb-d284-58ff-822b-0acb0718930c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/1c2ae1e58543ae6e9f26658ecbf416e399d7f56c5d38f0b17b4ac29dfc89920a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2442b6d9-06cb-5e4a-9536-6fff9833d38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/fe487e378dd633f91ee7cf1243312631695a5c750f8c0a0c888c9f2c86268ed3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379816} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b1b5ea0-1c31-5423-b6f5-af4705945147" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6851a9f5-d945-540b-94e8-2f205003c003" :question/math-academy-id "q-332941" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/7ad36c695bc150b580caa81f71fa358163a51ca3ed788dbd60e9cef980d9a75b.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point and go along with the flow (downward and slightly to the left) until the trajectory intersects the $y$-nullcline, where the tangents are horizontal.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/38cdd84fa7383122a41e287efe71822acc0ea6ffc7beb6567fe31e461e7b2bc2.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues going to the left but then starts turning upward.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/8861a2e90a1bf87651157b0eba1e38363f646c2305724a254498173fd47c554c.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues slightly to the left and upward, suggesting that it may converge to the origin.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073694/assets/a7c5a4702b6add4085b594d6e6cebd85b4746ef8138f22089679c5277266aa59.png)"}]}
